The whole-repository read-only regression snapshots every path, contents,
symlink target, mode, and timestamp under the worktree and the resolved Git
common directory before and after `doctor`, excluding only unavoidable external
Git lock implementation details if empirically observed and justified in the
test. It also snapshots refs, packed-refs, reflogs, FETCH_HEAD, index metadata,
and `.etude/` so a cache/write outside `.git` cannot pass. A stub remote provides
stable `ls-remote` reads without network writes.

## Verification

Before Verify gate: `gofmt` only the new/changed Go files; `make build`; focused
doctor tests; `make test`; `make lint`; `make docs`; `make docs-check`; and
`make docs-reality`. Because this is CLI-facing, also install with
`GOBIN=$PWD/.etude/tmp/etude-ldf/bin make install` and drive that exact installed
`etude doctor` against throwaway repositories covering a healthy
repo, dangerous legacy fetch, missing push, broken cross-reference, env/adapter
seat command with a missing real reviewer, missing rubric, unreachable remote,
and unpushed ref. Snapshot each throwaway repo before/after and clean it up.
